# skyline_deer_lake_ridge: the forested ridge above Deer Lake, on the way
# up to the Divide (BUILD_PLAN 4.4, S5 brief B3). A far-layer stamp: its
# anchor, 0,0, is its left end on the horizon line (a base's far_y plus the
# place's horizon), and it reaches 26 rows below it, under the near
# treeline, so a horizon shift never opens a gap (the composer's rule 3).
#
# A wooded ridge across the whole width in slate (2), the palette's far
# ridge: higher on the right toward Bogachiel, with two summits, the
# right one the higher, and a shallow saddle between them. Its crest is
# ragged with fir tips, spires a column wide and a row or two proud at
# uneven spacing, and bare at the two summits, where the first rocky
# outcrops stand: glacier blue (3) in the sun on the right, night navy (1)
# in shadow on the left, so the high country starts up there. No snow (the
# ridge is snow-free in August), nothing jagged beyond the trees: it must
# not compete with the lake.
#
# The ridge carries its own light: a level band of snow (4) behind its
# whole crest, its top a two-row checker seam into the sky (3.), drawn
# last, so the crest stands against the palest band at every hour (snow
# by day, alpenglow pink at dusk, glacier blue at blue hour, slate at
# night) while the ridge goes slate, navy, navy and ink (doc 11.4's key
# slots). The lake base keeps only a thin band over its trees, so a lake
# with no ridge gets open sky; this one brings its band where it stands,
# as the Olympus skyline does.
#
# At its foot, the haze, teal (15), the doc's hazy mid ridge: a lower
# spur's soft line, so the ridge never sits straight on the spruce
# treeline in front of it (at dusk slate goes navy and the treeline ink:
# the haze goes slate between them; at night ink over slate over the ink
# and navy treeline). It runs a pixel past each edge, so its fills cover
# the whole width and never reach the stamp's edge. Each band's outline
# goes first, then its fill from a seed inside.
#
# 1. The ridge, in slate: its crest of fir tips, down the sides a pixel
# off the canvas and along the bottom under the treeline, then its fill.
C 2  L -1,-12 0,-14 1,-12 2,-13 3,-14 4,-13 5,-15 6,-14
        8,-14 9,-16 10,-15 11,-16 12,-15 13,-16 14,-18 15,-16
        16,-16 17,-18 18,-17 19,-19 20,-18 22,-18 23,-20 24,-19
        25,-19 26,-20 27,-20 28,-22 29,-20 30,-20 31,-23 32,-21
        33,-22 36,-22 37,-24 38,-23 39,-24 40,-23 41,-24 42,-26
        43,-24 45,-24 46,-25 49,-25 50,-24 52,-24 53,-23 54,-25
        55,-22 56,-23 57,-22 58,-21 59,-22 60,-20 61,-21 62,-19
        63,-19 64,-18 65,-20 66,-18 67,-19 68,-17 69,-17 70,-18
        71,-17 72,-16 73,-18 74,-16 75,-18 76,-16 78,-16 79,-17
        80,-16 81,-17 82,-19 83,-17 84,-18 85,-17 86,-18 87,-20
        88,-18 89,-20 90,-18 91,-19 92,-19 93,-20 94,-20 95,-22
        96,-20 97,-21 98,-23 99,-22 100,-22 101,-23 102,-23 103,-25
        104,-24 106,-24 107,-26 108,-25 109,-26 110,-28 111,-26 112,-29
        113,-28 116,-28 117,-29 119,-29 120,-28 123,-28 124,-27 125,-27
        126,-29 127,-26 128,-26 129,-27 130,-26 131,-27 132,-25 133,-25
        134,-24 135,-26 136,-24 137,-24 138,-25 139,-23 140,-25 141,-23
        142,-22 143,-24 144,-22 145,-23 146,-22 148,-22 149,-23 150,-21
        151,-22 152,-21 153,-21 154,-23 155,-21 156,-20 157,-22 158,-20
        159,-21 160,-20 160,26 -1,26 -1,-12
C 2  F 80,0
# The outcrops at the two summits: each a knob of pale rock a few rows
# proud of the trees, its lit face glacier blue toward the sun on the
# right, its shadow face night navy on the left, drawn row by row, so no
# lone pixel reads as a speck.
C 1  L 47,-28  L 46,-27 47,-27  L 45,-26 47,-26  L 44,-25 46,-25
C 3  L 48,-28 49,-28  L 48,-27 50,-27  L 48,-26 52,-26  L 47,-25 53,-25
C 1  L 117,-32  L 115,-31 117,-31  L 114,-30 116,-30  L 113,-29 115,-29
C 3  L 118,-32 119,-32  L 118,-31 121,-31  L 117,-30 123,-30  L 116,-29 124,-29
C 1  L 126,-30  L 125,-29 126,-29
C 3  L 127,-30 128,-30  L 127,-29 129,-29
# 2. The haze at its foot: a lower spur's soft line, teal down under the
# treeline.
C 15  L -1,-6 4,-7 10,-8 16,-9 22,-9 28,-10 34,-11 40,-11 46,-10 52,-9
         58,-9 64,-8 70,-8 76,-9 82,-10 88,-10 94,-9 100,-8 106,-8
         112,-9 118,-10 124,-11 130,-12 136,-12 142,-11 148,-11 154,-10
         160,-10 160,26 -1,26 -1,-6
C 15  F 80,10
# 3. The horizon's light behind the crest: a bank of snow between slate
# walls a pixel off the canvas, filled down to the crest and around the
# outcrops, its top two rows a checker of snow and glacier blue (3) that
# seams it into the sky. Its edges go in first in colors that their fills
# then take: the seam's top row in paper cream (5), the row under the
# seam in alpenglow pink (6). The walls reach a row above the seam, so no
# fill touches the stamp's edge.
C 2  L -1,-37 -1,-12  L 160,-37 160,-20
C 5  L 0,-36 159,-36
C 6  L 0,-34 159,-34
C 4  F 80,-33 0,-34
D 4 3 checker  F 0,-35 0,-36
# The Look hotspot (S6): the ridge between its crest and the haze at its
# foot, across the whole width, in the stamp's coordinates. One hotspot and
# one alt part (alt.skyline.deer_lake_ridge) a skyline: every place that
# stands it is described and lookable.
Z ridge 0,-34,160,28
